Z||000000||Driven Visions||06-14-2001||09:10 PM||||My 84 fiero has a grille in the center and I see other models that have the grills on the sides<BR>Do all fieros with the grills on the sides have the hump shape by the back glass or are some of them flat||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||06-14-2001||09:17 PM||||Only 84s had the grill. 85-88 have the hump. No flat decklids. Also only 85-88 had the vents on the sides. 84s just had a flat non-vented piece on each side<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red (coming soon)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||06-14-2001||09:18 PM||||84's had the center grills, the hump was to make clearence for the V6??, but all deck lids can be interchanged. You can also use the vented side grills with the 84 lid.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||06-14-2001||10:11 PM||||Unless you get into fastbacks. They were flat, although with a complete raised portion down the middle. But they were all solid 'glass and not the metal vent thing like on the 84s... <P>And also are not interchangable with coupes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
